from pathlib import Path
import csv,datetime,hashlib,json,re
W=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2];A=W/'analysis/IV'
now=datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()
checker='GPT-6 Astra Pro (OpenAI, ChatGPT; current writing, 18 November 2026)'
refs=json.loads((A/'reference_checks.json').read_text())
data=[
 ('IV-R-030','AtiyahBott1984','Michael Atiyah and Raoul Bott',
  'Original Topology23(1984): Theorem3.5 p8; complete equivariant Euler-class argument, equations3.7 and3.8 p9',
  'https://www.math.stonybrook.edu/~mmovshev/MAT570Spring2008/BOOKS/atiyahbott_moment.pdf',
  'AtiyahBott1984.pdf',
  'Read and visually opened both original printed pages8–9. The push-pull i* i_* is multiplication by the equivariant Euler class; the normal representation has no fixed vectors, and its degree-zero-in-the-base Euler factor is the product of its nonzero weights. Localizing in those weights gives the explicit inverse sum of restriction divided by Euler class and the integration formula(3.8). This opens the exact localization formula used for the characteristic ledger; it assigns no proof credit to the individual ledger entries.'),
 ('IV-R-031','Satriano2012','Matthew Satriano',
  'Original Algebra&NumberTheory6(2012): Corollary1.8 p3; Proposition2.2 statement and full proof pp5–6',
  'https://msp.org/ant/2012/6-1/ant-v6-n1-p01-s.pdf',
  'Satriano2012.pdf',
  'Read and visually opened Corollary1.8 on p3 and Proposition2.2 on pp5–6. The former gives smoothness of the quotient at the image of a fixed point for a group generated by pseudoreflections, and its converse for stable groups. Proposition2.2 and its proof establish stability for finite constant groups, finite diagonalizable groups and the stated split connected-etale situation. The complex finite-group application therefore has the needed stable hypothesis. The entire proof of Corollary1.8 is not claimed as read; this is its exact theorem opening with the relevant stability proof.'),
 ('IV-R-032','Floyd1952','Edwin E. Floyd',
  'Original Trans.Amer.Math.Soc.72(1952): mod-p coefficient convention p139; Theorem4.4 and full proof p146',
  'https://scispace.com/pdf/on-periodic-maps-and-the-euler-characteristics-of-associated-1bgysb1nrr.pdf',
  None,
  'Opened the original ten-page AMS article scan through web retrieval and read the coefficient convention and full Theorem4.4 proof. Its prime-period fixed-set tail-sum inequality follows by descending induction in the special-homology exact sequence(A), followed by the inclusion of fixed-set homology in special homology. The receiving use is the n=0 total mod-p Betti inequality. Web retrieval identifiers turn745834230view3 and turn974705224view0 identify this opening. A local PDF fetch did not succeed; no local scan hash or completed visual inspection is asserted.')]
bibs=[W/'S6_10_PAPERS_references.bib',W/'papers/IV/references_additions.bib']
for eid,key,author,locator,url,filename,check in data:
 assert not any(x['event_id']==eid for x in refs),eid
 sources=[str(p.relative_to(W.parents[1])) for p in bibs if re.search(r'@\w+\{'+re.escape(key)+r'\s*,',p.read_text())]
 assert sources,key
 if filename:
  pdf=A/'references'/filename;assert pdf.is_file()
  check+=' PDF SHA256 '+hashlib.sha256(pdf.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
 refs.append(dict(event_id=eid,bib_key=key,bib_aliases=[],author=author,locator=locator,
  source=url,check=check,checker=checker,recorded_at=now,
  bib_key_sources={key:sources},bib_key_match_scope='Exact author/title/publication identity. Current reading credit is confined to the stated original-edition loci.',bib_key_matched_at=now))
(A/'reference_checks.json').write_text(json.dumps(refs,indent=2)+'\n')
cols=['event_id','bib_key','bib_aliases','author','locator','source','check','checker','recorded_at']
with (A/'reference_checks.tsv').open('w',newline='') as f:
 w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=cols,delimiter='\t');w.writeheader()
 for r in refs:w.writerow({k:json.dumps(r[k],ensure_ascii=False) if isinstance(r.get(k),(list,dict)) else r.get(k,'') for k in cols})
print(json.dumps(dict(recorded_at=now,reference_events=len(refs))))
